4,\"_genreOverlap\":1},{\"id\":2472,\"title\":\"The Apprentice\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/cUflI3B1Bmzxba8xgplyEnozaLt.jpg\",\"rating\":5.9,\"year\":2005,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.41304347826086957,\"_genreOverlap\":1},{\"id\":283312,\"title\":\"George Clarke's Building Home\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/ejrtmpjtcqhU4pmnXuShbxM1m38.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"year\":2025,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.411764705882353,\"_genreOverlap\":1}],\"seasonNumber\":7,\"seasonName\":\"Season 7\",\"seasonOverview\":\"\",\"seasonPoster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/AnWebNmI7sM9bYNlfPuDhvraxaI.jpg\",\"seasonAirDate\":\"2010-01-14\",\"episodes\":[{\"number\":1,\"name\":\"Back to New York\",\"overview\":\"Season 7 of Project Runway premieres with sixteen new designers, who will try to make their way to Bryant Park to show their collections at Fashion Week. The contestants are asked to create a garment that represents who they are as a designer. They must  choose five fabrics from a wide selection provided by Mood and have one day to complete their look.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/4bTNvKitlJJKl4vvwWoQTKvz2YU.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":2,\"airDate\":\"2010-01-14\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":2,\"name\":\"The Fashion Farm\",\"overview\":\"The designers must create a party look from a burlap potato sack for their model/clients. They are given the raw materials and have one day to complete the challenge.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/wRjxCqoeYpppQmRop5mKe0JJs34.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":2,\"airDate\":\"2010-01-21\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":3,\"name\":\"The Hi's and Lows of Fashion\",\"overview\":\"After being taken to the Metropolitan Museum of Art for inspiration from famous designers, the contestants are then divided into teams of two. The challenge is to create a high-end signature look worthy of a master collection. They have $500 and two days to complete their looks. The next day, they are given the additional task of creating a second \\\"look for less,\\\" using only 10% of the budget for the first garment and inspired by the look being crafted by another team.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/b3bdH1AMmHkNop4Oc1me3i61l3y.jpg\",\"rating\":7,\"voteCount\":2,\"airDate\":\"2010-01-28\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":4,\"name\":\"Design Your Heart Out\",\"overview\":\"The designers are asked to design a look for a Fashion Week gala featuring the color red and elements of Campbell's Soup branding. They have $100 and one day to finish the design. Lisa Walker - VP of Innovation, Campbell's Soup.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/87O63raaP9eFGrre69bA7TPsnOz.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":2,\"airDate\":\"2010-02-04\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":5,\"name\":\"Run For Cover\",\"overview\":\"The designers must create a look to be worn by Heidi Klum on the cover of Marie Claire magazine. They have $150 and one day to complete the challenge.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/bPWNf5wy86n2Dd6lDJGldGoei1w.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":2,\"airDate\":\"2010-02-11\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":6,\"name\":\"A Little Bit of Fashion\",\"overview\":\"The designers must design an outfit for a child model. They have $50 and one day to complete their looks. The next morning, Tim gives them the additional task of designing a companion outfit for their adult models. They are given an additional $100 and one more day to complete the challenge.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/A4ZIjEFpW41nY04G3G14xIKBNYc.jpg\",\"rating\":7,\"voteCount\":2,\"airDate\":\"2010-02-18\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":7,\"name\":\"Hard Wear\",\"overview\":\"The designers get the task of creating an unconventional, innovative look and a matching accessory from materials found at a hardware store. They have $150 and one day to complete the challenge.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/ssHCjtOKOuR4KV0VpAG8LLAkpi2.jpg\",\"rating\":4.5,\"voteCount\":4,\"airDate\":\"2010-03-04\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":8,\"name\":\"The Elements of Fashion\",\"overview\":\"The designers are asked to create a look inspired by one of the four classical elements (Earth, Water, Air, and Fire). They have $150 and one day to complete their garments.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/dtCt4ob206W1lMnsMIHlvBgtHhP.jpg\",\"rating\":7,\"voteCount\":2,\"airDate\":\"2010-03-11\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":9,\"name\":\"Takin' It to the Streets\",\"overview\":\"Working in teams of two, the designers must create a day look and an evening look after finding inspiration in iconic neighborhoods of New York (Harlem, Upper East Side, Chinatown, and East Village). They have $300 and one day to complete the challenge.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/4v2luMP6ExBuUVylos02lpzrDXH.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":2,\"airDate\":\"2010-03-18\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":10,\"name\":\"Hey, That's My Fabric\",\"overview\":\"The designers must create their looks with their own digitally-printed fabric that they create themselves. They have $100 for additional materials and two days to complete their garments.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/gR6lbe1YT41RrOtYkx577A9D93y.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":2,\"airDate\":\"2010-03-25\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":11,\"name\":\"Sew Much Pressure\",\"overview\":\"The contestants must craft a red carpet design for Heidi Klum. They have $300 and one day to complete their looks.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/405uoqzlu3EkLkDbGO5iC7qjjFV.jpg\",\"rating\":6,\"voteCount\":3,\"airDate\":\"2010-04-01\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":12,\"name\":\"The Big, Top Designers\",\"overview\":\"The designers are asked to create a high-end look inspired by the Ringling Brothers and Barnum & Bailey Circus. They have $300 and two days to complete their outfits.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/6ZsyCH4BzyoxoWlPN6dkZ9T5u4z.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":2,\"airDate\":\"2010-04-08\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":13,\"name\":\"Finale: Part 1\",\"overview\":\"Each of the remaining designers is given four months and $9000 to design a 10-piece collection for Fashion Week. In the interim, each gets a special visit in their hometown from Tim Gunn. Back in New York, two designers must compete head-to-head for the last spot in the finale.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/iV2C962Lm6fsMTRycSd9yLfScjH.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":2,\"airDate\":\"2010-04-15\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":14,\"name\":\"Finale: Part 2\",\"overview\":\"In the conclusion of the finale, the remaining contestants ready their collections for the runway. Then they present their lines to industry insiders at Fashion Week.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/mrCdZTypGlKQzwKifgTgLsjQOdI.jpg\",\"rating\":9,\"voteCount\":2,\"airDate\":\"2010-04-22\",\"runtime\":43}],\"firstAirDate\":\"2004-12-01\"}","status":200,"url":""},"revalidate":86400,"tags":[]}